        "mechanism": "Hurdle-rate economics. When short-term risk-free Treasury yields sit near 4.5–4.8%, the cash return exceeds the implied earnings yield of equity repurchases or inflated private equity deal multiples. Buffett’s rule dictates that buybacks destroy intrinsic value when executed above conservative appraisal thresholds.",
        "strategicImpact": "Serves as a bellwether for institutional asset allocation. Berkshire is signaling that public equity markets are priced for perfection and private M&A valuations have not yet adjusted to structurally higher cost-of-capital regimes.",
        "coreLesson": "Cash is an active strategic call option, not an idle balance-sheet drag. When asset valuations are overextended, preserving liquidity generates asymmetric upside during eventual market dislocations.",
